# COS-1051 — Android upload-signing secrets. NEVER commit these.
#
# `keystore.properties` holds the store and key passwords in plaintext, and
# `upload.keystore` is the signing key itself. Together they are everything
# needed to sign a release as us.
#
# They were never committed, but nothing on main stopped it: the ignore rules
# lived only on the parked COS-1037 branch, so a `git add -A` here would have
# taken both. That is not hypothetical in this repo — COS-742 committed dev
# build config to main exactly that way, and COS-1032 repeated it.
#
# Losing the upload key is recoverable (Google support can reset it); leaking
# it is not, because anyone holding it can sign an artifact that Play accepts
# as ours.
android/keystore.properties
android/app/upload.keystore
android/app/*.keystore
android/app/*.jks
